rce":"derivative","format":"PNG","original":"Westwood - LWR - April 1985.mp3","mtime":"1605903365","size":"38534","md5":"033d087d6898f47e57a77791211e5cec","crc32":"b779fd4d","sha1":"099606dc4d7fd4fb3f38025d79172f822e6f4b81"},{"name":"Westwood - LWR - April 1985_spectrogram.png","source":"derivative","format":"Spectrogram","original":"Westwood - LWR - April 1985.mp3","mtime":"1605903388","size":"279488","md5":"cd540f6cb35652d2058d7f78c0d1059e","crc32":"6786040e","sha1":"9bc01b7045b23a7062670fc779c6db876faad0bc"},{"name":"__ia_thumb.jpg","source":"original","mtime":"1605903444","size":"3650","md5":"69a98cc98ee4e7d725309d7aae3a025d","crc32":"e58c8b0d","sha1":"ef4e1a5f4dc0bffbd425c0a75803ccc9205a7506","format":"Item Tile","rotation":"0"}],"files_count":9,"item_last_updated":1605911932,"item_size":73355599,"metadata":{"identifier":"TheHipHopShow-198504","mediatype":"audio","collection":["hiphopradioarchive","radioprograms"],"creator":"Tim Westwood","date":"1985-04","description":"<div>This is gold school for any and all aging b-boys, and anyone that tuned into pirate radio in the UK during the 80s.</div><div><br /></div><div>This tape is from April 1985. Love him or loathe him, just listen to the sound of Tim's voice and maybe you’ll get a better idea of where he started, how much he seemed to care, what he has done, and how much he has developed over the years.</div><div><br /></div><div><div>This show was kindly donated by a gentleman commonly referred to as the nicest guy in UK Hip-Hop. Head photographer [and ex-colleague] for the longest running monthly periodical devoted entirely to Hip-Hop, all round Rap oracle Paul Hampartsoumian, AKA Paul H.</div><div><br /></div><div>During the 80s, the pages of <i>HHC </i>were plastered with iconic images from Normski, but when the 90s came along, Paul’s work would’ve unquestionably caught your eye. Whether it was a recognizable front cover, the VISUALS of the London club scene or pretty much every Rap gig that took place in the capital during the decade, Paul got a shot of it and it appeared in <i>Hip-Hop Connection</i> [Big shouts to our old editor Andy Cowan]</div></div><div><br /></div><div><b>Track List</b></div><div><ul><li>Run DMC – You Talk Too Much<br /></li><li>Run DMC – Sucker MCs</li><li>Mic Break</li><li>Sparky Dee Vs The Playgirls ‎– The Battle</li><li>Mic Break</li><li>Mighty Mouth ‎- All Wrapped Out</li><li>Mic Break</li><li>James Brown – I’m Satisfied</li></ul><div>- Irish Craig @ RandomRap Radio (track list assist: Deejay Mek)</div></div>","language":"eng","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.4","subject":["hip-hop","radio","london","pirate radio","lwr","westwood"],"title":"The Hip-Hop Show (Westwood LWR): April 1985","uploader":"rmacmich@gmail.com","publicdate":"2020-11-20 20:14:27","addeddate":"2020-11-20 20:14:27","year":"1985","hhra_title":"The Hip-Hop Show","hhra_callletters":"LWR","hhra_stationfreq":"92.5 FM","hhra_location":"London, England, UK","hhra_djshosts":"Tim Westwood","hhra_credit":"Paul H, Irish Craig - RandomRapRadio","hhra_sourceurl":"https://randomrapradio.com/2020/11/19/tim-westwood-on-lwr-from-april-september-1985-remastered/"},"server":"ia601807.us.archive.org","uniq":1745782214,"workable_servers":["ia601807.us.archive.org","ia801807.us.archive.org"]}